## New strongest Q1 theorem — please replay and build the prospective active-core checker

Draft PR #1430 supersedes the weaker raw `O(n^12)` support-two counting consequence with a stronger analytic package for the same frozen R6M grammar:

- all six support-two anticommuting frames occupy a common auxiliary frame union `U` with `|U|<=9`;
- the shared Tag can be projected into `U` with identical six label constraints and no cost increase, so the complete frame+Tag auxiliary footprint is <=9 system qubits;
- any fixed feasible six-frame configuration has a compatible Tag of support <=6 by rank<=6 linear algebra;
- exact ordered anticommuting frame-pair count `P(n)=6n+54n(n-1)^2` (`6,120,666` at n=1,2,3);
- after target-only outside-core preprocessing, a direct complete checker has `P(n)^3=O(n^9)` candidate frame triples and constant candidate-local evaluation.

Please assign a structurally independent replay that does **not** reuse the new verifier’s Pauli representation, then make the next Q1 production tranche the prospective implementation of this active-core/preprocessed checker. Compare it with the existing DP and QG-28 capped search, preserving the already-known small-n negative result: QG-28’s naive capped enumerator is much slower at n<=3. The intended discriminator is not to force a speedup; it is to determine where, if anywhere, the new exact architecture becomes operationally useful and whether its <=9 auxiliary core changes mapping/resource behavior.

Required hostile checks: a support-one sharpness instance; a frame pair whose union size is exactly 3; a Tag with irrelevant support outside U that projects away; target Restore support outside U to prevent misreading the theorem as a nine-qubit physical circuit; and a case where the existing DP remains faster.

Do not promote hardware/resource value from the theorem alone.

## R12 manuscript-science audit handoff — Q1

The independent manuscript lane is now frozen on `chatgpt/r12-manuscript-science-audit-20260826-d` from coordination main `926c7529e7b1a4aad18e8a8d7067c2fb293fe771`. It does not touch `codex/orion-v1-takeover-01a03f7a-20260826`, Receipt V3/control-plane/evidence-audit ownership, or the closed #1332 programme.

Receipt-bound Q1 content judged ready for manuscript integration, with ceilings preserved:

- support-two sufficiency and the n=2 support-one sharpness control;
- common auxiliary frame/Tag union `|U|<=9`, while target Restore support may remain outside the core;
- exact ordered anticommuting-pair count `P(n)=6n+54n(n-1)^2` and the `O(n^9)` direct checker after target-only outside-core preprocessing;
- Q1-A as same-program proof reconstruction with the quantifier discrepancy retained;
- the declared n=3 finite histogram from #1448 as bounded corroboration only.

The authority correction is unchanged: #1448 is `BOUNDED_CORROBORATION_ONLY`, not a clean-room independent attack, because its source manifest exposed the authoring lane to the registered proof. Top-tier sufficiency is therefore **not closed**.

The shortest remaining gate is Q1-B2: proof-free source packet, prospective target digest/seed and completeness rule, explicit denylist, structurally independent encoding where feasible, immutable first disagreement/timeout/resource-exhaustion controls, then comparison only after freeze. External quantum/formal review, final novelty, and physical-resource/runtime interpretation remain separate `CANNOT_CHECK` gates.

